{
  "dom_id": "step-q132624",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The time $X,$ in seconds, between two students arriving at a canteen can be modeled as an exponential random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.05).$ If a student has just arrived at the canteen, what is the average time until the next student arrives there?",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{\\lambda }.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(0.05).$ Therefore, $\\lambda =0.05,$ and\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{0.05}\\,\\text{sec}=20\\,\\text{sec}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average time until the next student arrives is $20$ seconds.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
